Boston lets you view models in different languages, e.g. Entity Relationship Diagrams and Property Graph Schemas. Each language view of the model is within a Page within the model.
\par 
\par Boston currently supports the following languages:
\par 
\par 1. Object-Role Models;
\par 2. Entity Relationship Diagrams;
\par 3. Property Graph Schemas;
\par 4. State Transition Diagrams;
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs22\insrsid2967002 Unified Modelling
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid2967002 
\par The different language views, as Pages, are unified within Boston and changing the name or properties of a model element within one language automatically changes the relevant model element in the related language.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid2967002 NB}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid2967002  The primary language in Boston is Obj
