\par 
\par 
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s4\ql \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\tx1200\wrapdefault\faauto\outlinelevel3\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs24\ul\lang1252\langfe3081\cgrid\langnp1252\langfenp3081 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid2967002 {\*\bkmkstart topic_Code_Generator_Statement_CNum}{\*\bkmkend topic_Code_Generator_Statement_CNum}CNum
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang3081\langfe3081\cgrid\langnp3081\langfenp3081 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid2967002 
Convert expression to numeric.
\par 
\par This is useful for mathematical expressions where you want to avoid string concatenation if a variable\rquote s type is a string.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid2967002 Definition
