The CREATE DATABASE statement allows you to create a database (SQLite at this stage) that is connected to a Model in Boston.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs26 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs26\insrsid2967002 Syntax
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid2967002 
\par CREATEDATBASESTATEMENT ::= CREATE DATABASE <ModelDatabaseName>; LOCATIONCLAUSE [;TYPECLAUSE]
\par 
\par \tab ModelDatabaseName : The name of the Model that will be created, and the name of the database.
\par 
\par LOCATIONCLAUSE ::= LOCATION = <Disk drive location>
\par 
\par \tab Disk drive location : The location on the computer disk where the database will be created. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid2967002 \tab NB}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid2967002  Must include the name of the database file. E.g. MyModel.db
\par 
\par TYPECLAUSE ::= TYPE = <DatabaseType>
\par 
\par \tab DatabaseType : Limited to 'SQLite' at this stage.
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\s1\ql \li0\ri0\keepn\widctlpar\tx1200\wrapdefault\faauto\outlinelevel0\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs24\ul\lang1252\langfe3081\cgrid\langnp1252\langfenp3081 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid2967002 {\*\bkmkstart topic_The_ORM_Studio_Database}{\*\bkmkend topic_The_ORM_Studio_Database}The Boston Database
\par 
\par }\pard\plain \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 \rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs24\alang1025 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs24\lang3081\langfe3081\cgrid\langnp3081\langfenp3081 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid2967002 
The Boston database contains a state of the art MetaModel of Fact-Based Modeling (FBM). The following help topics describe the tables and fields of the Fact-Based Modeling MetaModel within Boston.
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\fs20\insrsid2967002 NB}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid2967002  Tables that are prefixed, 'MetaModel', are at the MetaM
etaModel level of a 4-Layer Architecture when considering Languages interpreted from the Model (stored within the MetaModel) that are not ORM or FBM Models. Tables that are prefixed 'Model' are at the MetaModel level of a 4-Layer Architecture when conside
ring Languages interpreted from the Model (stored within the MetaModel) that are not ORM or FBM Models.
\par 
\par The languages currently supported by Boston are Object-Role Modeling (ORM), Entity Relationship Diagrams, Property Graph Schema and State Transition Dia
grams. Boston's 4-Layer Architecture supports Languages other than ORM to be stored within the one ORM MetaModel as MetaMetaModel.
\par 
